4. Core Product Invariants

The following rules form the product’s operational contract:

No valid identity or authority
    → no governed decision.
No eligible evidence
    → no retrieval.
No durable retrieval admission
    → no retrieval.
No verified completed retrieval
    → no governed context.
No governed context
    → no generation.
No validated output
    → no execution.
No durable proof
    → no successful governance claim.

All failure paths must be explicit and fail closed.

An error, missing state, stale policy, expired assignment, ambiguous scope, failed receipt write, or unverifiable evidence must never silently degrade into an allow decision.

