10. Canonical Runtime Stages

S0 — Request Ingress

Responsibilities:

* normalize request;
* create requestId;
* validate request structure;
* prepare verified identity input.

S0 performs no policy decision and no retrieval.

⸻

S1 — Authority Resolution / DAR

Responsibilities:

* consume verified identity;
* resolve customerId;
* require explicit activeScopeId;
* resolve active assignment;
* resolve role;
* enforce customer boundary;
* produce deterministic AuthoritySnapshot;
* produce deterministic state hash;
* return typed denial on failure.

DAR must not:

* query vector databases;
* evaluate semantic similarity;
* call LLMs;
* retrieve content;
* evaluate prompt meaning.

⸻

S2 — Governance

Inputs:

* AuthoritySnapshot;
* requested action;
* purpose;
* environment;
* resource context;
* policy snapshot;
* current time.

Controls:

* role;
* classification;
* temporal validity;
* retention;
* legal hold;
* approval;
* source type;
* topic restrictions.

Output:

GovernanceContext

including:

* decision;
* typed reasons;
* authority hash;
* policy hash;
* classification ceiling;
* permitted scopes;
* source restrictions;
* approval state;
* issued time;
* expiry.

S2 does not retrieve information.

